The Postulo name and logo
-------------------------
postulo-mcp is a companion tool of Postulo, made by the same project and installed beside
the agent rather than into an instance. It carries Postulo's own logo as its own: it is
the same mark, not a lookalike.

  assets/postulo-logo.svg
      Postulo's vector mark, byte for byte the file at assets/brand/postulo.svg in
      https://source.tiagoagueda.com/postulo/postulo (sha256
      94ff1200270fa49927feeda473b7e61f42bf1ad37b4baf89ffb63bcbd333bfb7).

  src/postulo_mcp/assets/postulo-logo-256.png
      Postulo's own 256 px raster of it, byte for byte the file at
      src/postulo/static/brand/logo-256.png in the same repository (sha256
      695d2c4c60ab2492423c85af688c5706950d9f2bfba2069523f6ba2413ee9366). It lives inside the
      package, as a plugin's logo does, so an installed copy carries it too.

The name Postulo and this logo are NOT covered by the AGPL. They belong to the Postulo
project, and TRADEMARKS.md in the Postulo repository says what that means and what you may
do without asking, which is nearly everything: run this, fork it, redistribute it unmodified
under its own name, and say truthfully that something works with Postulo. If you distribute
a materially modified postulo-mcp, give it another name and another logo, or say plainly and
near the name that it is modified and not endorsed by Postulo. The files above are not
modified here, and a test holds them to the checksums in this notice.

